{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791376207226,"sessionID":"ses_ee9a86284ffedma3YbQXzblH8I","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_6xxiHVZ6wAfzXYqLjlVY2809","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/brief.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n2: \n3: type: feature\n4: id: punishment\n5: branch: feature/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: author: Leander Muskalla\n8: \n9: ## What\n10: \n11: When I'm browsing the link library and I select a category, e.g. \"Tech\" and then add a new link, I'd expect that link to also land in that category I'm currently looking at. However, it adds it without any categories / Uncategorized.\n12: \n13: ## Why\n14: \n15: <!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n16: \n17: ## Out of scope\n18: \n19: <!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n20: \n21: ## Notes\n22: \n23: <!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>\n\n<system-reminder>\nInstructions from: /workspace/docs/AGENTS.md\n# solyto frontend\n\n<!--\nThis is your project context, loaded by the agent at the start of every session.\nmanigot is vendor-agnostic: it runs Claude Code or OpenCode against the same\nproject (`mg --profile claude-pro` vs `mg --profile zai`/`--profile\nopencode-go`), and this one file serves both — manigot mounts it read-only\nwherever the selected tool looks for it\n(/workspace/AGENTS.md for OpenCode, /workspace/.claude/CLAUDE.md for Claude\nCode). Those mount paths are read-only: to change this context, edit this\nfile (docs/AGENTS.md), never the mount paths.\nThe same global agents are available under @name either way, and custom\nproject agents in docs/agents/ work under both tools — write them in the\nbuilt-in format (name:, description:, tools: Read, Grep, ...), no per-tool\nformat needed. To make a custom agent read-only under OpenCode, add a\n`permission:` frontmatter block (the built-in format manigot's conversion\npasses through to OpenCode's schema — see the manigot README's agent section);\nthe read-only built-in agents' blocks deny the destructive git commands\n(worktree management, branch -d/-D, reset, checkout, push, ...).\nCustom agents that must commit (like the built-in developer/reviewer/quality)\ndeclare `commit: true` in their frontmatter; agents that never commit declare\n`commit: false` and get a read-only git mount. The default — no agent named,\nfile missing, or marker absent/unknown — is a writable git mount, so a\ncommitting agent is never broken by a missing marker.\nAgent sessions also restrict git to reading history and making commits (the\nsession git shim): worktree management, branch deletes, resets, checkouts,\npushes, and the other destructive subcommands are refused.\nKeep this file tool-neutral — write it for \"the agent\", not for one vendor.\n-->\n\nThe client for [solyto.app](https://solyto.app): a free, private, all-in-one personal management app — todos, notes, calendar, contacts, media libraries, check-in, finances, feeds, time tracking, clipboard, and dev-requests in one place. This repo is the frontend only: a SvelteKit 2 / Svelte 5 single-page app that runs on the web, as an installable PWA, or as a native desktop/mobile shell. There is no backend or database here — every piece of data comes from the solyto REST API, which lives in a separate repository.\n\n## Stack\n- Backend: none in this repo — pure client-side SPA. Consumes the solyto REST API at `/api/v1` (`api.solyto.app` in prod, `http://localhost:8000` in dev; configurable per hostname in `src/lib/config/platform.ts`).\n- Frontend: SvelteKit 2, Svelte 5 (runes, `$state`), TypeScript (strict), Vite 7, Tailwind CSS v4 via `@tailwindcss/vite`, adapter-node (outputs to `build/`).\n- Database: none — persistence is owned by the backend. The client only stores auth tokens, theme, and preferences in LocalStorage (`src/lib/services/LocalStorageService.ts`).\n- Key packages: `@tiptap/*` (notes rich-text editor), `echarts` (statistics charts), `@simplewebauthn/browser` (passkey login), `marked` + `dompurify` (markdown), `@lucide/svelte` (icons), `svelte-dnd-action` / `svelte-gestures` (drag & drop, swipe), `canvas-confetti`, `@fontsource/*`, `@vvo/tzdb`.\n\n## Architecture\n- `src/routes/` — SvelteKit file-based routes, all client-rendered (no `+page.server.ts`/`+server.ts` anywhere). The root `+layout.svelte` bootstraps every state store via `setContext`, guards unauthenticated access (redirect to `/auth/login` or `/setup`), and renders the navbar/footer shells. Feature routes: `/todos`, `/notes`, `/calendar`, `/contacts`, `/check-in`, `/finances`, `/feeds`, `/time-tracking`, `/clipboard`, `/dev-requests`, `/libraries/{books,movies,music,games,links,quotes,recipes,plants}`, plus `/settings`, `/admin`, `/profile`, `/auth/*`, `/setup`, `/share`.\n- `src/lib/state/` — one Svelte 5 runes class per domain (`Auth`, `Todos`, `Notes`, `Calendars`, `BookLibrary`, ...). Instances are created in `+layout.svelte` and shared through Svelte context (`setContext`/`getContext`); each store fetches via `ApiService` and holds the result in reactive `$state`.\n- `src/lib/services/` — `ApiService` (fetch wrapper over the REST API: Bearer auth, JSON, `%s`/`%d` URL placeholders, FormData uploads) and pure domain services (`TodoFilterService`, `TodoSortingService`, `TodoGroupingService`, `TodoRelevanceService`, `LibraryFilterService`, `WealthStatisticsService`, ...) that are unit-tested.\n- `src/lib/config/` — `apiRoutes.ts` (all endpoints, composed from `getApiUrl()` + `/api/v1`), `platform.ts` (web vs. desktop vs. mobile via `PUBLIC_DESKTOP`/`PUBLIC_MOBILE`, API URL resolution), `themes.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `urls.ts`, `features.ts`.\n- `src/lib/components/` — feature components plus shared `ui/` (buttons, modals, navbar), `forms/` (inputs, pickers, toggles), and `charts/` (echarts wrappers). Several features keep separate desktop/mobile view variants (e.g. `calendars/views/{day,week,month,list}`, `todos/views/`).\n- `src/lib/types/` — TypeScript interfaces mirroring the API data model, one file per domain (`todo.ts`, `note.ts`, `library_*.ts`, `calendar.ts`, ...).\n- `src/lib/i18n/` — translation tables `en.ts`, `de.ts`, `es.ts`, `fr.ts`, typed via `types/translation.ts`; every UI string must exist in all four.\n- `src/lib/helpers/` — pure utilities (DateHelper, NumberHelper, FormatHelper, ColorHelper, MusicTheory, ...).\n- `src/service-worker.ts` — PWA service worker (app-shell precache, stale-while-revalidate, push notifications); `static/site.webmanifest` is the PWA manifest, `static/themes/*` are runtime-loaded theme CSS.\n- `tests/` — Vitest unit tests for pure helpers/services only (no component or integration tests); run in node env with `TZ=UTC` and `$lib` aliased to `src/lib`.\n- Data flow: component → state store → `ApiService` → REST API. There is no server-side rendering of app data.\n\n## Commands\n- `npm run dev` — start the Vite dev server on port 5173 (expects the API at `http://localhost:8000`)\n- `npm run build` — production build via `vite build` (adapter-node, output in `build/`)\n- `npm run preview` — preview the production build locally\n- `npm run check` — type-check with `svelte-check` (a11y warnings selectively ignored)\n- `npm run lint` — `prettier --check .` + `eslint .`\n- `npm run format` — auto-format with `prettier --write .`\n- `npm test` / `npm run test:watch` — run Vitest unit tests / watch mode\n- `make deploy` / `make audit` — Ansible deploy (external `deployment/` repo) / `npm audit` + `npm outdated`\n\n## Hard rules\n- NEVER modify files outside /workspace\n- NEVER install packages without asking (dependencies are pinned, `engine-strict=true`)\n- NEVER commit secrets: auth tokens, API keys, or `.env*` files (gitignored); never log or print token or user data\n- NEVER hand-edit generated output — `build/` and `.svelte-kit/` are regenerated by `npm run build` / `npm run check`\n- When adding or changing UI strings, keep all four i18n files (`en`, `de`, `es`, `fr`) in sync — `npm run check` enforces it\n- When scope is unclear: ask, don't guess\n- Do not refactor things unrelated to the current task\n- Do not add abstractions not already present in the codebase\n\n</system-reminder>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\ntype: feature\nid: punishment\nbranch: feature/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category\ndate: 2026-10-07\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nWhen I'm browsing the link library and I select a category, e.g. \"Tech\" and then add a new link, I'd expect that link to also land in that category I'm currently looking at. However, it adds it without any categories / Uncategorized.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n","truncated":false,"loaded":["/workspace/docs/AGENTS.md"],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/brief.md","text":"# Brief: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\ntype: feature\nid: punishment\nbranch: feature/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category\ndate: 2026-10-07\nauthor: Leander Muskalla\n\n## What\n\nWhen I'm browsing the link library and I select a category, e.g. \"Tech\" and then add a new link, I'd expect that link to also land in that category I'm currently looking at. However, it adds it without any categories / Uncategorized.\n\n## Why\n\n<!-- Why does this need to exist? What problem does it solve for the user? -->\n\n## Out of scope\n\n<!-- What are we explicitly NOT doing in this job? -->\n\n## Notes\n\n<!-- Anything the analyst or developer should know before starting. -->","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/brief.md","time":{"start":1791376207089,"end":1791376207181}},"id":"prt_11657aca50018L6Wv91l7Ng10q","sessionID":"ses_ee9a86284ffedma3YbQXzblH8I","messageID":"msg_11657a17100101ZBiiMsHVgOtd"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791376207226,"sessionID":"ses_ee9a86284ffedma3YbQXzblH8I","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_G7flfiaq5bsH7hXP04LE0301","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n2: \n3: id: punishment\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Context / findings\n11: \n12: The bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n13: \n14: - `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n15:   request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n16:   regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n17: - The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n18:   (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n19:   `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n20:   - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)\n21:   - `0`    = \"Uncategorized\" tab (line 56)\n22:   - positive number = a real category id (line 85)\n23:   - `'favorite'` = favourites tab (line 30)\n24: - `LinkLibrary.create()` calls `load()`, which calls `reapplyFilter()`, so once\n25:   the new link is saved under the selected category it will already appear in\n26:   the current view — no extra refresh logic is needed.\n27: - Existing precedent for \"inherit the active filter on create\" already exists\n28:   in the codebase: `Todos.quickCreate()` sets `request.category_id` from the\n29:   active category filter (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` lines 268-275). The\n30:   links fix should follow the same idea.\n31: - Other callers of `LinkLibrary.create()` must NOT change behaviour:\n32:   `src/lib/components/feeds/SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` saves feed items with\n33:   an explicit `category_id: null` and gets a *separate* `LinkLibrary` instance\n34:   from `/feeds/+layout.svelte` whose `activeFilter` is never set (stays `null`).\n35:   A store-level default keyed off `activeFilter` therefore leaves it untouched,\n36:   but the developer must confirm this and keep it true.\n37: \n38: Expected mapping for a newly created link, given the active filter:\n39: `positive category id -> that id`; `0 | null | 'favorite' -> null`\n40: (uncategorized). \"All\" stays uncategorized to preserve current behaviour.\n41: \n42: ## Task breakdown\n43: \n44: TASK-1: Make a new link inherit the currently selected category.\n45:   files: src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts,\n46:          src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte\n47:   depends: none\n48:   risk: low — single-purpose mapping; needs care only so the feeds save path\n49:         (activeFilter null, separate store instance) still sends null.\n50:   detail:\n51:     - Add a small method on `LinkLibrary` (e.g. `getActiveCategoryId(): number | null`)\n52:       that returns the active filter when it is a positive number, else `null`.\n53:       This mirrors the existing small getters `getCategoryCount()` /\n54:       `getFavoriteCount()` and makes the logic unit-testable (the repo has no\n55:       component tests).\n56:     - In `LinkCreate.svelte` `onsubmit()`, replace the hardcoded\n57:       `category_id: null` with the value returned by that method.\n58:     - Do not change `LinkLibrary.create()`'s signature or the\n59:       `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` caller.\n60: \n61: TASK-2: Add regression tests for the active-category mapping.\n62:   files: tests/unit/stores/LibraryStores.test.ts\n63:   depends: TASK-1\n64:   risk: low — additive tests against the `LinkLibrary` describe block.\n65:   detail:\n66:     - Cover each filter state: real category id -> that id; `0`\n67:       (uncategorized) -> null; `'favorite'` -> null; `null` (all) -> null.\n68:     - Follow the existing `new LinkLibrary()` setup and `filterByCategory()` /\n69:       `filterByFavorite()` usage already in this file (lines 512-593).\n70: \n71: TASK-3: Verify the change end to end.\n72:   files: (no source changes; produces command output only)\n73:   depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n74:   risk: low — standard project checks.\n75:   detail:\n76:     - `npm run check` (type-check; no i18n keys are added by this change).\n77:     - `npm test` (Vitest unit tests).\n78:     - `npm run lint`.\n79:     - Manual/rendered confirmation that adding a link while a category is\n80:       selected lands it in that category, and that the \"All\" / \"Uncategorized\"\n81:       / favourites tabs still create uncategorized links.\n82: \n83: ## Out of scope\n84: \n85: - Any change to `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` / the feeds save flow (it has no\n86:   category context and must keep saving uncategorized).\n87: - The mobile layout: `CategoryHeader.svelte` is `max-md:hidden`, so there is no\n88:   category selection UI on small screens to inherit; not part of this brief.\n89: - Adding a category picker to the create modal — the brief only asks for the\n90:   currently-browsed category to be preselected.\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\nid: punishment\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / findings\n\nThe bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n\n- `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n  request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n  regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n- The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n  (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n  `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n  - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\nid: punishment\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / findings\n\nThe bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n\n- `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n  request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n  regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n- The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n  (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n  `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n  - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)\n  - `0`    = \"Uncategorized\" tab (line 56)\n  - positive number = a real category id (line 85)\n  - `'favorite'` = favourites tab (line 30)\n- `LinkLibrary.create()` calls `load()`, which calls `reapplyFilter()`, so once\n  the new link is saved under the selected category it will already appear in\n  the current view — no extra refresh logic is needed.\n- Existing precedent for \"inherit the active filter on create\" already exists\n  in the codebase: `Todos.quickCreate()` sets `request.category_id` from the\n  active category filter (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` lines 268-275). The\n  links fix should follow the same idea.\n- Other callers of `LinkLibrary.create()` must NOT change behaviour:\n  `src/lib/components/feeds/SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` saves feed items with\n  an explicit `category_id: null` and gets a *separate* `LinkLibrary` instance\n  from `/feeds/+layout.svelte` whose `activeFilter` is never set (stays `null`).\n  A store-level default keyed off `activeFilter` therefore leaves it untouched,\n  but the developer must confirm this and keep it true.\n\nExpected mapping for a newly created link, given the active filter:\n`positive category id -> that id`; `0 | null | 'favorite' -> null`\n(uncategorized). \"All\" stays uncategorized to preserve current behaviour.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Make a new link inherit the currently selected category.\n  files: src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts,\n         src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte\n  depends: none\n  risk: low — single-purpose mapping; needs care only so the feeds save path\n        (activeFilter null, separate store instance) still sends null.\n  detail:\n    - Add a small method on `LinkLibrary` (e.g. `getActiveCategoryId(): number | null`)\n      that returns the active filter when it is a positive number, else `null`.\n      This mirrors the existing small getters `getCategoryCount()` /\n      `getFavoriteCount()` and makes the logic unit-testable (the repo has no\n      component tests).\n    - In `LinkCreate.svelte` `onsubmit()`, replace the hardcoded\n      `category_id: null` with the value returned by that method.\n    - Do not change `LinkLibrary.create()`'s signature or the\n      `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` caller.\n\nTASK-2: Add regression tests for the active-category mapping.\n  files: tests/unit/stores/LibraryStores.test.ts\n  depends: TASK-1\n  risk: low — additive tests against the `LinkLibrary` describe block.\n  detail:\n    - Cover each filter state: real category id -> that id; `0`\n      (uncategorized) -> null; `'favorite'` -> null; `null` (all) -> null.\n    - Follow the existing `new LinkLibrary()` setup and `filterByCategory()` /\n      `filterByFavorite()` usage already in this file (lines 512-593).\n\nTASK-3: Verify the change end to end.\n  files: (no source changes; produces command output only)\n  depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n  risk: low — standard project checks.\n  detail:\n    - `npm run check` (type-check; no i18n keys are added by this change).\n    - `npm test` (Vitest unit tests).\n    - `npm run lint`.\n    - Manual/rendered confirmation that adding a link while a category is\n      selected lands it in that category, and that the \"All\" / \"Uncategorized\"\n      / favourites tabs still create uncategorized links.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` / the feeds save flow (it has no\n  category context and must keep saving uncategorized).\n- The mobile layout: `CategoryHeader.svelte` is `max-md:hidden`, so there is no\n  category selection UI on small screens to inherit; not part of this brief.\n- Adding a category picker to the create modal — the brief only asks for the\n  currently-browsed category to be preselected.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":90,"totalLines":90,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791376207194,"end":1791376207206}},"id":"prt_11657ad10001hCz0mZ8aFdoMkR","sessionID":"ses_ee9a86284ffedma3YbQXzblH8I","messageID":"msg_11657a17100101ZBiiMsHVgOtd"}}
