{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791376549171,"sessionID":"ses_ee9a33476ffek46vS2h4uJeqKA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_5MnfwYJdvvnwadGWMLNX3611","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n2: \n3: id: punishment\n4: status: open\n5: analyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\n6: date: 2026-10-07\n7: \n8: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n9: \n10: ## Context / findings\n11: \n12: The bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n13: \n14: - `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n15:   request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n16:   regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n17: - The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n18:   (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n19:   `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n20:   - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)\n21:   - `0`    = \"Uncategorized\" tab (line 56)\n22:   - positive number = a real category id (line 85)\n23:   - `'favorite'` = favourites tab (line 30)\n24: - `LinkLibrary.create()` calls `load()`, which calls `reapplyFilter()`, so once\n25:   the new link is saved under the selected category it will already appear in\n26:   the current view — no extra refresh logic is needed.\n27: - Existing precedent for \"inherit the active filter on create\" already exists\n28:   in the codebase: `Todos.quickCreate()` sets `request.category_id` from the\n29:   active category filter (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` lines 268-275). The\n30:   links fix should follow the same idea.\n31: - Other callers of `LinkLibrary.create()` must NOT change behaviour:\n32:   `src/lib/components/feeds/SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` saves feed items with\n33:   an explicit `category_id: null` and gets a *separate* `LinkLibrary` instance\n34:   from `/feeds/+layout.svelte` whose `activeFilter` is never set (stays `null`).\n35:   A store-level default keyed off `activeFilter` therefore leaves it untouched,\n36:   but the developer must confirm this and keep it true.\n37: \n38: Expected mapping for a newly created link, given the active filter:\n39: `positive category id -> that id`; `0 | null | 'favorite' -> null`\n40: (uncategorized). \"All\" stays uncategorized to preserve current behaviour.\n41: \n42: ## Task breakdown\n43: \n44: TASK-1: Make a new link inherit the currently selected category.\n45:   files: src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts,\n46:          src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte\n47:   depends: none\n48:   risk: low — single-purpose mapping; needs care only so the feeds save path\n49:         (activeFilter null, separate store instance) still sends null.\n50:   detail:\n51:     - Add a small method on `LinkLibrary` (e.g. `getActiveCategoryId(): number | null`)\n52:       that returns the active filter when it is a positive number, else `null`.\n53:       This mirrors the existing small getters `getCategoryCount()` /\n54:       `getFavoriteCount()` and makes the logic unit-testable (the repo has no\n55:       component tests).\n56:     - In `LinkCreate.svelte` `onsubmit()`, replace the hardcoded\n57:       `category_id: null` with the value returned by that method.\n58:     - Do not change `LinkLibrary.create()`'s signature or the\n59:       `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` caller.\n60: \n61: TASK-2: Add regression tests for the active-category mapping.\n62:   files: tests/unit/stores/LibraryStores.test.ts\n63:   depends: TASK-1\n64:   risk: low — additive tests against the `LinkLibrary` describe block.\n65:   detail:\n66:     - Cover each filter state: real category id -> that id; `0`\n67:       (uncategorized) -> null; `'favorite'` -> null; `null` (all) -> null.\n68:     - Follow the existing `new LinkLibrary()` setup and `filterByCategory()` /\n69:       `filterByFavorite()` usage already in this file (lines 512-593).\n70: \n71: TASK-3: Verify the change end to end.\n72:   files: (no source changes; produces command output only)\n73:   depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n74:   risk: low — standard project checks.\n75:   detail:\n76:     - `npm run check` (type-check; no i18n keys are added by this change).\n77:     - `npm test` (Vitest unit tests).\n78:     - `npm run lint`.\n79:     - Manual/rendered confirmation that adding a link while a category is\n80:       selected lands it in that category, and that the \"All\" / \"Uncategorized\"\n81:       / favourites tabs still create uncategorized links.\n82: \n83: ## Out of scope\n84: \n85: - Any change to `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` / the feeds save flow (it has no\n86:   category context and must keep saving uncategorized).\n87: - The mobile layout: `CategoryHeader.svelte` is `max-md:hidden`, so there is no\n88:   category selection UI on small screens to inherit; not part of this brief.\n89: - Adding a category picker to the create modal — the brief only asks for the\n90:   currently-browsed category to be preselected.\n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\nid: punishment\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / findings\n\nThe bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n\n- `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n  request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n  regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n- The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n  (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n  `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n  - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: link library: with a category selected add to that category\n\nid: punishment\nstatus: open\nanalyst: deepseek-v4-flash (analyst)\ndate: 2026-10-07\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Context / findings\n\nThe bug is a hardcoded value, not a missing feature.\n\n- `src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte` builds the create\n  request in `onsubmit()` and always sends `category_id: null` (line 44),\n  regardless of which category the user is currently viewing.\n- The current selection lives in `LinkLibrary.activeFilter`\n  (`src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts` line 35), typed\n  `null | number | 'favorite'`:\n  - `null` = \"All\" tab (CategoryHeader line 17)\n  - `0`    = \"Uncategorized\" tab (line 56)\n  - positive number = a real category id (line 85)\n  - `'favorite'` = favourites tab (line 30)\n- `LinkLibrary.create()` calls `load()`, which calls `reapplyFilter()`, so once\n  the new link is saved under the selected category it will already appear in\n  the current view — no extra refresh logic is needed.\n- Existing precedent for \"inherit the active filter on create\" already exists\n  in the codebase: `Todos.quickCreate()` sets `request.category_id` from the\n  active category filter (`src/lib/state/Todos.svelte.ts` lines 268-275). The\n  links fix should follow the same idea.\n- Other callers of `LinkLibrary.create()` must NOT change behaviour:\n  `src/lib/components/feeds/SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` saves feed items with\n  an explicit `category_id: null` and gets a *separate* `LinkLibrary` instance\n  from `/feeds/+layout.svelte` whose `activeFilter` is never set (stays `null`).\n  A store-level default keyed off `activeFilter` therefore leaves it untouched,\n  but the developer must confirm this and keep it true.\n\nExpected mapping for a newly created link, given the active filter:\n`positive category id -> that id`; `0 | null | 'favorite' -> null`\n(uncategorized). \"All\" stays uncategorized to preserve current behaviour.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\nTASK-1: Make a new link inherit the currently selected category.\n  files: src/lib/state/LinkLibrary.svelte.ts,\n         src/lib/components/libraries/links/LinkCreate.svelte\n  depends: none\n  risk: low — single-purpose mapping; needs care only so the feeds save path\n        (activeFilter null, separate store instance) still sends null.\n  detail:\n    - Add a small method on `LinkLibrary` (e.g. `getActiveCategoryId(): number | null`)\n      that returns the active filter when it is a positive number, else `null`.\n      This mirrors the existing small getters `getCategoryCount()` /\n      `getFavoriteCount()` and makes the logic unit-testable (the repo has no\n      component tests).\n    - In `LinkCreate.svelte` `onsubmit()`, replace the hardcoded\n      `category_id: null` with the value returned by that method.\n    - Do not change `LinkLibrary.create()`'s signature or the\n      `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` caller.\n\nTASK-2: Add regression tests for the active-category mapping.\n  files: tests/unit/stores/LibraryStores.test.ts\n  depends: TASK-1\n  risk: low — additive tests against the `LinkLibrary` describe block.\n  detail:\n    - Cover each filter state: real category id -> that id; `0`\n      (uncategorized) -> null; `'favorite'` -> null; `null` (all) -> null.\n    - Follow the existing `new LinkLibrary()` setup and `filterByCategory()` /\n      `filterByFavorite()` usage already in this file (lines 512-593).\n\nTASK-3: Verify the change end to end.\n  files: (no source changes; produces command output only)\n  depends: TASK-1, TASK-2\n  risk: low — standard project checks.\n  detail:\n    - `npm run check` (type-check; no i18n keys are added by this change).\n    - `npm test` (Vitest unit tests).\n    - `npm run lint`.\n    - Manual/rendered confirmation that adding a link while a category is\n      selected lands it in that category, and that the \"All\" / \"Uncategorized\"\n      / favourites tabs still create uncategorized links.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- Any change to `SaveToLibraryButton.svelte` / the feeds save flow (it has no\n  category context and must keep saving uncategorized).\n- The mobile layout: `CategoryHeader.svelte` is `max-md:hidden`, so there is no\n  category selection UI on small screens to inherit; not part of this brief.\n- Adding a category picker to the create modal — the brief only asks for the\n  currently-browsed category to be preselected.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":90,"totalLines":90,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/punishment_link-library-with-a-category-selected-add-to-that-category/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791376549074,"end":1791376549163}},"id":"prt_1165ce4550013uvbtIJ0a05WhG","sessionID":"ses_ee9a33476ffek46vS2h4uJeqKA","messageID":"msg_1165cdc19001Pj9Ok7EuRXNwul"}}
